// SideNav: an app's side navigation, drawn as its own panel. Width, with no breakpoint (Exact has no media
// query): the panel and an empty, zero-tall spacer share a wrapping row — the panel's basis blocks.nav-min, the
// spacer's blocks.nav-page-min (the least room a page beside the rail needs) and a thousandfold grow. Where both
// fit (a desktop, a tablet) the spacer takes the rest and the panel stands as a rail of its basis; where they do
// not (a phone, or a shell's own sidebar column) the spacer wraps away and the panel fills the whole width, a
// full-width list; narrower than its basis it shrinks (min-width 0) and the rows' own truncation holds.
//
// Height is the shell's, and the panel meets it half way: given a definite height the panel's own spacer grows
// and the account pins to its bottom. Alone in a window the panel is as tall as what it holds plus the list's
// own room — measured twice and probed again (`forma-kind`: a library forma admits only px, rem, em or a named
// length, so no viewport unit; a percentage height resolves against the harness's content-tall mount), so a
// panel alone in a window cannot pin its account to that window, and no shell should be asked to. What the
// panel can hold by itself is its own geometry: the places area reserves its room (blocks.nav-places-min, the
// height of the starter's own full menu, measured from the resting panel) in every state, so the footer, the
// brand and the slot sit in one place whether the menu is full, long, one, loading, empty or failed — the
// envelope is the constant, the content is what changes. Two look rounds went opposite ways on reserved air
// when the samples were five rows (one dinged a compact card for the empty window below it — space the shots
// harness owns; the next read a centered card's reserved home as "skeleton rows removed but their space not
// collapsed"); with a real menu's samples the resting panel itself fills the window, and the next round asked
// for exactly this: "the shell keeps its geometry in every state". The floor is a minimum, not a height: a real
// shell's pane taller than the panel grows the spacer; and the panel closes with a full hairline frame, so it
// reads as one finished panel and never as a surface cut off against the page — the frame also carries the
// theme-safe rule (a theme may give page and surface one colour, so a panel never relies on its fill alone to
// show its edges).
//
// One gutter holds everything: the panel pads by theme.space.sm and every word inside pads its start by
// theme.space.md, so the brand's mark, a group's heading, each place's label, a state's words and the account
// all start on one edge; the state cards' corners sit on that same edge (their columns pad the same md), so a
// state never reads as a different component from the list that surrounds it — while a row's fill (the current
// place's, a hover's) spans the panel's own content width, measured: both hairlines and every row fill span one
// grid edge (a look round claimed the brand's and the account's dividers span differently; they do not, and
// this note keeps the next reader from chasing it). Grouping is by space — a heading, then its rows,
// theme.space.xs between every one of them; the air between groups, theme.space.lg, the only larger gap — not
// by frames; the line token draws the panel's own frame, the hairline that closes the brand and the one above
// the account, and nothing else.
//
// - The brand is its own region, the same height in every state: the product's mark and name (each optional by
//   being empty, the name the panel's largest words) and the hairline that closes it. The slot (the app's
//   control: a switch, a search) opens the places' area under the hairline, in a bay bounded by
//   blocks.nav-slot-bay: the bay grows to its bound and never past it — a control fits with air around it, and
//   what the app puts there beyond two body lines scrolls inside the bay rather than pushing the menu down
//   (measured in the long cell: two full lines show, the third stays inside the scroll), so the places start one
//   even rhythm after whatever the app gives. A look round read ~90px of air between the slot's words and the
//   first group: that was the bay holding a fixed two-line height around one line of filler — a bounded bay no
//   longer reserves air it does not need.
// - The places: NavEntry rows grouped by `group` in first-seen order ("" no heading); a group's own name is its
//   heading, an eyebrow — the caption type, muted, one step under every place's body, so the sections read as
//   names of rooms, not as rows. The current place is the panel's one filled thing, and selection is one device
//   in the accent's ink: a flush hair at the row's start (drawn over the fill and clipped by the row's corner,
//   so the label keeps the gutter every other word starts on), the label's heavier type, the fill,
//   aria-current="page" — the agent's mark stays its own drawing, a rounded edge set in from the row, with its
//   note. A badge counts, one treatment in both schemes and on every row (the current one too): an outline
//   chip, a hairline and a count in theme.color.ink-muted (light #63636b on white ~5.9:1, dark #a1a1aa on
//   surface ~7:1 — and the hairline shows on the current row's fill, where the old surface-on-fill pill vanished
//   in dark); a count is worth reading at a glance, but it is metadata, so it never competes with the accent; a
//   row with no count keeps the count's room, so every label holds its line on the same edge.
// - An agent that added or reordered an entry (agent "changed"): the entry `agentKey` names gets an accent edge
//   at its start and `agentNote`'s words under its label (the kit's LinkRow language).
// - The states' words speak where the rows speak — no heading of their own, so a state never reads as a copy
//   change — and each state stands at the top of the list's own room: the brand, the slot, the room, the
//   account, in one stack.
// - Loading says its line once — a small drawn cue beside muted words (role=status) — above the shape coming:
//   three sections as the resting list has, each a short bar for the group's own label on a section-label row
//   (md tall, as a real label is; a look round read sm-tall head ghosts as "no section-header placeholders"),
//   then word-wide label bars for its rows, and where the row will carry a count, the badge's own ghost at the
//   row's far end — where the badge itself stands, never a second bar beside the word (a look round read the
//   near-badge ghosts as "stray pills") — mirroring the resting sample, badge for badge. Bars are the width of
//   a word, not lines the width of the panel, on the rows' own pitch (blocks.nav-row-min and the xs gap, the
//   resting rhythm exactly), so what arrives does not jump and the ghosts read as labels coming, not as rules
//   across the rail.
// - Failed speaks the kit's outcome language, theme-safe: the words and the drawn mark in the error's ink on
//   the surface token (status words never sit on a tinted fill — another party's theme may not hold 4.5:1
//   there), the frame a critical hairline on the surface, the mark above the message so the message holds the
//   card's whole width and never wraps a widow ("could not be / loaded." was the look round's reading of a
//   212px column), and `retryLabel`'s button drawn plain below the message — the one control in the card is the
//   way on, and no second hue competes with the error's voice. Empty is its neutral twin: the line's own hair,
//   and `emptyLabel`'s button drawn primary when the app gives one — the panel has no accent of its own in that
//   state, so the way on is the one filled thing in it.
// - The landmark's name, `navLabel`, is what a reader hears; the words a person sees above the rows are the
//   data's own group names.
// - Long: everything the panel draws holds one line with an ellipsis, and every line that can be cut carries
//   the whole of itself as its `title` (the kit's affordance for a cut line — a reader hovers the row, the
//   name, or the account's byline and the full words appear); the account's role a short byline
//   (blocks.nav-role-max), never a second sentence racing the name; the slot's content is the app's, bounded by
//   the bay, and a package cannot clamp what it does not draw.
//
// States:
//   data   many|empty|loading|failed|long|one
//   agent  none|changed
use Words, ActionButton from "__SCOPE__/components"

// One place in the navigation: `group` names the section it sits in ("" for none), `badge` counts what it holds
// (0 hides the chip), `current` marks the place the person is on.
shape NavEntry
  key: string
  label: string
  href: string
  group: string
  badge: number
  current: bool

// A group's heading, at the rows' own inset: the places' sections, and the only section words the panel shows.
// An eyebrow: the caption type, muted, one step under the places' body.
component NavHeading
  props
    text: string
    testId: string
  view
    text text testId=testId font="theme.type.caption" color="theme.color.ink-muted" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"

// One place: its label on one line (an ellipsis a whole gap before its count; a row with no count keeps the
// count's room, so every label in the panel holds its line on the same edge), the current place's fill and
// weight, an agent's edge and note. The label's `title` carries the whole of it for a line the panel cuts.
component NavItem
  props
    label: string
    href: string
    badge: number
    current: bool
    marked: bool
    note: string
    testId: string
  view
    link href=href testId=testId aria-current=(current ? "page" : "false") position="relative" display="flex" flex-direction="row" align-items="center" gap="theme.space.lg" min-height="blocks.nav-row-min" box-sizing="border-box" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" padding-top="theme.space.xs" padding-bottom="theme.space.xs" overflow="hidden" border-radius="theme.radius.control" color="theme.color.ink" text-decoration-line="none" background-color=(current ? "theme.color.fill" : "transparent")
      :hover
        background-color="theme.color.hover"
      :active
        background-color="theme.color.fill"
      :focus-visible
        box-shadow="inset 0 0 0 2px theme.color.focus"
      if current
        box position="absolute" left=0 top=0 bottom=0 width="blocks.nav-mark-line" background-color="theme.color.accent" aria-hidden=true
      if marked
        box position="absolute" left=0 top="theme.space.sm" bottom="theme.space.sm" width="blocks.nav-mark-line" background-color="theme.color.accent" border-radius="theme.radius.pill" aria-hidden=true
      column flex=1 min-width=0 padding-right=(badge > 0 ? "0" : "blocks.nav-count-space")
        text label title=label font=(current ? "theme.type.label" : "theme.type.body") color=(current ? "theme.color.accent" : "theme.color.ink") white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"
        if marked
          text note title=note testId=`${testId}-mark` font="theme.type.caption" color="theme.color.accent" white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"
      if badge > 0
        row testId=`${testId}-badge` flex-shrink=0 min-width="blocks.nav-badge-min" box-sizing="border-box" justify-content="center" align-items="center" padding-left="theme.space.sm" padding-right="theme.space.sm" border-width="theme.line.width" border-style="solid" border-color="theme.color.ink-muted" border-radius="theme.radius.pill"
          text `${badge}` font="theme.type.caption" color="theme.color.ink-muted" font-variant-numeric="tabular-nums" white-space="nowrap"

// A group's own label, still coming: a short bar the width of a shorter word (shorter than a place's bar, as a
// heading is) at the heading's inset, md tall as a real label is, on a row the height of a section label — so
// the section that arrives takes the place its ghost held, close to its rows the way a real heading sits.
component NavHeadGhost
  view
    row min-height="theme.space.xl" align-items="center" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" aria-hidden=true
      box width="blocks.nav-ghost-head" height="theme.space.md" background-color="theme.color.fill" border-radius="theme.radius.pill"

// A place still coming: the row's own height and insets, a bar the width of a word where the label will be and,
// where the row will carry a count, the badge's own ghost at the row's far end — where the badge itself stands,
// never a second bar beside the word — so what arrives does not jump.
component NavGhost
  props
    badge: bool
  view
    row align-items="center" gap="theme.space.lg" min-height="blocks.nav-row-min" box-sizing="border-box" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" padding-top="theme.space.xs" padding-bottom="theme.space.xs" aria-hidden=true
      box width="blocks.nav-ghost-word" height="theme.space.lg" background-color="theme.color.fill" border-radius="theme.radius.pill"
      if badge
        column flex=1
        box width="blocks.nav-ghost-badge" height="theme.space.lg" flex-shrink=0 background-color="theme.color.fill" border-radius="theme.radius.pill"

component SideNav
  props
    productName: string
    productMark: string
    navLabel: string
    entries: NavEntry[]
    data: enum<"many", "empty", "loading", "failed", "long", "one">
    emptyText: string
    emptyLabel: string
    empty: action
    loadingText: string
    failedText: string
    retryLabel: string
    retry: action
    accountName: string
    accountDetail: string
    agent: enum<"none", "changed">
    agentKey: string
    agentNote: string
    testId: string
  slot
  derive names = entries.map(e => e.group)
  derive groups = names.filter((g, i) => names.indexOf(g) == i)
  view
    row flex-wrap="wrap" align-items="stretch"
      column testId=testId role="navigation" aria-label=navLabel flex-grow=1 flex-shrink=1 flex-basis="blocks.nav-min" min-width=0 box-sizing="border-box" gap="theme.space.lg" padding="theme.space.sm" background-color="theme.color.surface" border-width="theme.line.width" border-style="solid" border-color="theme.color.line"
        row align-items="center" gap="theme.space.sm" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" padding-top="theme.space.sm" padding-bottom="theme.space.sm" border-bottom-width="theme.line.width" border-bottom-style="solid" border-bottom-color="theme.color.line"
          if productMark != ""
            column width="blocks.nav-mark" height="blocks.nav-mark" flex-shrink=0 background-color="theme.color.fill" border-radius="theme.radius.control" justify-content="center" overflow="hidden" aria-hidden=true
              text productMark.trim().slice(0, 2) font="theme.type.heading" color="theme.color.ink" text-align="center" white-space="nowrap"
          if productName != ""
            text productName testId=`${testId}-name` title=productName flex=1 min-width=0 font="theme.type.title" color="theme.color.ink" white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"
        column min-width=0 max-height="blocks.nav-slot-bay" overflow="auto" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md"
          children
        column min-width=0 min-height="blocks.nav-places-min"
          if data == "failed"
            column padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md"
              row role="alert" background-color="theme.color.surface" border-width="theme.line.width" border-style="solid" border-color="theme.color.critical" border-radius="theme.radius.control"
                column flex=1 min-width=0 gap="theme.space.sm" padding="theme.space.md"
                  svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="blocks.nav-glyph" height="blocks.nav-glyph" fill="none" stroke="theme.color.critical-text" aria-hidden=true flex-shrink=0
                    path d="M12 3.5 L21 19 h-18 z" stroke-width=1.75 stroke-linejoin="round"
                    path d="M12 9.5 v4.5" stroke-width=1.75 stroke-linecap="round"
                    path d="M12 16.6 v0.2" stroke-width=1.75 stroke-linecap="round"
                  column flex=1 min-width=0
                    Words(text=failedText, kind="body", outcome="error", level=0, testId=`${testId}-${data}`)
                  row
                    ActionButton(label=retryLabel, kind="plain", interaction="idle", outcome="none", press=retry, testId=`${testId}-retry`)
          else if data == "loading"
            column gap="theme.space.lg"
              row role="status" align-items="center" gap="theme.space.sm" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md"
                svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="blocks.nav-cue" height="blocks.nav-cue" fill="none" aria-hidden=true flex-shrink=0
                  path d="M12 3.5 A8.5 8.5 0 1 1 3.5 12" stroke="theme.color.ink-muted" stroke-width=2.5 stroke-linecap="round"
                column flex=1 min-width=0
                  Words(text=loadingText, kind="body", outcome="cancelled", level=0, testId=`${testId}-${data}`)
              column aria-hidden=true gap="theme.space.xs"
                NavHeadGhost()
                NavGhost(badge=false)
                NavGhost(badge=true)
                NavGhost(badge=false)
                NavGhost(badge=false)
              column aria-hidden=true gap="theme.space.xs"
                NavHeadGhost()
                NavGhost(badge=false)
                NavGhost(badge=true)
                NavGhost(badge=false)
              column aria-hidden=true gap="theme.space.xs"
                NavHeadGhost()
                NavGhost(badge=true)
                NavGhost(badge=false)
                NavGhost(badge=false)
          else if data == "empty"
            column padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md"
              row role="status" background-color="theme.color.surface" border-width="theme.line.width" border-style="solid" border-color="theme.color.line" border-radius="theme.radius.control"
                column flex=1 min-width=0 gap="theme.space.md" padding="theme.space.md"
                  Words(text=emptyText, kind="body", outcome="cancelled", level=0, testId=`${testId}-${data}`)
                  if emptyLabel != ""
                    row
                      ActionButton(label=emptyLabel, kind="primary", interaction="idle", outcome="none", press=empty, testId=`${testId}-add`)
          else
            column gap="theme.space.lg"
              for g in groups key=g
                column gap="theme.space.xs"
                  if g != ""
                    NavHeading(text=g, testId=`${testId}-group-${g}`)
                  column gap="theme.space.xs"
                    for e in entries.filter(e => e.group == g) key=e.key
                      NavItem(label=e.label, href=e.href, badge=e.badge, current=e.current, marked=(agent == "changed" and e.key == agentKey), note=agentNote, testId=`${testId}-entry-${e.key}`)
        column flex=1 min-height="0"
        if accountName != ""
          row testId=`${testId}-account` align-items="center" gap="theme.space.md" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" padding-top="theme.space.md" padding-bottom="theme.space.xs" border-top-width="theme.line.width" border-top-style="solid" border-top-color="theme.color.line"
            column width="theme.space.xxl" height="theme.space.xxl" flex-shrink=0 background-color="theme.color.fill" border-radius="theme.radius.pill" align-items="center" justify-content="center" overflow="hidden" aria-hidden=true
              text accountName.trim().slice(0, 1) font="theme.type.label" color="theme.color.ink"
            column flex=1 min-width=0
              text accountName title=accountName font="theme.type.label" color="theme.color.ink" white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"
              if accountDetail != ""
                text accountDetail title=accountDetail max-width="blocks.nav-role-max" font="theme.type.caption" color="theme.color.ink-muted" white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"
      box flex-grow=1000 flex-shrink=1 flex-basis="blocks.nav-page-min" height=0 aria-hidden=true
